Run the GitHub credential helper with Omnigent's own Python.

The per-user broker helper written to ~/.gitconfig ran bare python3. Runner
login shells put mise's shims first on PATH, so in a project that pins Python
(.mise.toml, .tool-versions) python3 was the project's interpreter, which has
no omnigent module, and git push/fetch to github.com failed. The helper now
names sys.executable, e.g. /opt/venv/bin/python3. The host rewrites the helper
on every start, so existing sessions pick it up when they wake.
Base: omnigent v0.15.0 (c8b9b85f822f).

diff --git a/omnigent/git_credential_github.py b/omnigent/git_credential_github.py
index 8d7ca07..472e337 100644
--- a/omnigent/git_credential_github.py
+++ b/omnigent/git_credential_github.py
@@ -146,8 +146,11 @@ def _install_broker_helper(server_url: str, host_id: str, token: str) -> None:
     re-runs on every resume). A plain set can't overwrite the 2+ values that
     leaves, so without ``--replace-all`` broker entries would pile up.
     """
+    # The interpreter running this, not whatever ``python3`` is on PATH: in a
+    # project that pins Python with mise, the shims put a Python without
+    # omnigent first, and every git operation against github.com would fail.
     helper = (
-        "!python3 -m omnigent.git_credential_github "
+        f"!{shlex.quote(sys.executable)} -m omnigent.git_credential_github "
         f"--server {shlex.quote(server_url)} --host-id {shlex.quote(host_id)} "
         f"--host-token {shlex.quote(token)}"
     )
